The license above covers plastron's own files: the build, its packages
(splash, jackswitch, powerkey, mesa3d-px2), the init scripts, the scripts and
the docs. Third-party files in this repository keep their own licenses:

  buildroot/board/px2/patches/linux/
                   Patches to the Linux kernel, from ROCKNIX and from
                   kernel.org, and our own. GPL-2.0, as the kernel is.

  buildroot/board/px2/dts/
                   The Pixel 2 device tree, from ROCKNIX, (c) GameKiddy and
                   Rockchip. GPL-2.0+ OR MIT, as each file states.

  buildroot/board/px2/linux.config.rocknix
                   ROCKNIX's kernel config for the RK3326, which
                   scripts/kernel-config.sh starts from.

  buildroot/board/px2/u-boot/
                   Patches and sources for U-Boot, from ROCKNIX and
                   Hardkernel, and our own. GPL-2.0+, as U-Boot is.

  buildroot/board/px2/bootloader/
                   ROCKNIX's bootloader, and ours with U-Boot rebuilt.
                   Both carry Rockchip's prebuilt DDR init, miniloader and
                   BL31, redistributed as ROCKNIX does, under Rockchip's
                   terms (github.com/rockchip-linux/rkbin).

  buildroot/package/splash/frames.bin
                   TortOS's boot animation, from TortOS. MIT.

The card image the build produces contains much more than this repository:
the kernel, U-Boot, BusyBox, glibc, Mesa, SDL and the rest, each under its
own license. Buildroot gathers them, with their sources, by
`make legal-info`; each release carries that alongside the image.
